     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (850 mg three times daily). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max dose.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1000 mg per dose.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is intended, please confirm that. I'd also suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Once you reply, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
